  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "In a closed system, $\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{s}) \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{~B}(\\mathrm{~g})+3 \\mathrm{C}(\\mathrm{g})$, if partial\r\n\r\npressure of $\\mathrm{C}$ is doubled, then partial pressure of $\\mathrm{B}$ will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iqMfB",
      "text": "$2 \\sqrt{2}$ times the original value",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vj1ia",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2}$ times the original value",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "z3vqr",
      "text": "2 times the original value",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PBFNP",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}}$ times the original value",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad K_{p}=p_{B_{1}}^{2} \\times p_{C_{1}}^{3}$\r\n\r\nAgain, $K_{p}=p_{B_{2}}^{2} \\times\\left(2 p_{C_{1}}\\right)^{3}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{B}_{1}}^{2} \\times \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{C}_{1}}^{3}=\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}_{2}}^{2} \\times 8 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{C}_{1}}^{3}$\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\frac{\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{B}_{1}}^{2}}{8}=\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{B}_{2}}^{2} \\text { or, } \\frac{\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{B}_{1}}}{2 \\sqrt{2}}=\\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{B}_{2}}\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
